  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "TL;DR: Add a search bar to the top of the options menus.\nThe UI has come a long way from the days of the past, when the settings were only the place you went to tweak your height, mic settings, and tell new users where to turn off that setting that makes other people vanish when you're closer than a metre. Now it is full of pages and pages of options, and we can only expect the number of options to go up in response to new features and user feedback.\nSome people will advocate for moving options around, shuffling them from one place to another that \"makes more sense\". But what's good for different people will be quite different, and things that make semantic sense will be different between one person and another. It also doesn't help in the case where a setting is added in beta and shoved into the bottom of a mystery list. Overall, just moving things around won't help with situations where you want to find a specific setting but don't know where it is. And there are so many settings in new and different places which often rarely need changing that most people aren't going to remember where they are to help people even if they wanted to! \nSo, here's my suggestion - add a search bar to the top of the options menu. This is pretty common among modern UIs, from televisions to smartphones. Other parts of the menu are already searchable, so adding more search bars would be a great touch and improve usability greatly.",
